 "notes": "Review by Mostepanenko & Klimchitskaya summarizing the authors' own constraints on the axion-nucleon coupling from Casimir-effect experiments (GUT axions/ALPs, two-axion exchange). Curve is the lower envelope of Figure 8 lines 1 (Casimir-less experiment, strongest for m_a < 0.9 eV), 2 (Casimir pressure, 0.9-8 eV), 3 (lateral Casimir force, 8-17.8 eV) and 'new' (Casimir force at nanometer separations, Au sphere vs SiC plate, > 17.8 eV), extracted from the vector EPS figVMM-8.eps in the e-print. Axis calibration verified against text-quoted crossings at 0.9, ~8 and 17.8 eV. Figure plots g_an^2/(4pi); reported g_an = sqrt(4pi * y). Paper assumes g_an = g_ap (axion-to-nucleon); reported as AxionNeutron with the same value applying to protons. The paper's g_an is the dimensionless pseudoscalar coupling entering V = g_an^2/(16 pi m^2)[...] (Eq. 11), identical to the canonical dimensionless g_an; no 2m_N conversion needed. Experimental errors determined at 95% CL. Envelope displayed from m_a = 1e-3 eV (frame edge in Figs 6 and 8) to 100 eV. Not a dark-matter search; density-independent (fifth-force/two-axion-exchange lab limit).",
